      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the safe limit for acetaminophen.\n\n- **Daily total:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6 g/day. The usual maximum for adults is 4 g/day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 1000 mg.\n- **Risk:** At 6 g/day, the risk of hepatotoxicity is significant, even with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some options that stay within the limits:\n- 1000 mg by mouth three times daily (3 g/day)\n- 1000 mg by mouth four times daily (4 g/day, the maximum)\n- 650 mg by mouth every 6 hours (2.6 g/day)\n\nIf you meant a different dose or frequency, tell me and I'll enter it. If you really do want 2000 mg three times daily, tell me that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose."
      }
     ],
